  | **Customization** | Limited (ChatGPT memory + custom GPTs planned); API fine-tuning via Azure | Claude Recall (private knowledge ingestion); Agent Teams (multi-agent coding preview); fine-tuning in partnership | Copilot Studio for custom assistants; Power Automate flows; can’t fine-tune GPT directly (but Azure OpenAI allows fine-tuning) | Wide (Vertex AI fine-tuning, custom Vertex Agents); Gemini Agent SDK (Beta) |
  | **Knowledge Access** | Chat Plugins (e.g. Slack, Jira); Azure Cognitive Search | Project workspaces, document uploads | Microsoft Graph (e.g. Outlook, SharePoint); 3rd-party connectors (Salesforce app) | Connectors to Workspace, Teams, Gmail, plus M365/Graph via Teams connector; external APIs via Agent |
  | **Pricing** | Custom (contact sales) ( [\[31\]](https://www.techtarget.com/searchenterpriseai/definition/What-is-ChatGPT-Enterprise-Pricing-uses-and-features#:~:text=The%20Enterprise%20version%2C%20however%2C%20does,which%20is%20the%20tier%20below "Highlights: The Enterprise version, however, does,which is the tier below")); likely >$30/user/mo (est.) | Custom enterprise contracts (not publicly listed) | GitHub Copilot: $19/user/mo ( [\[46\]](https://docs.github.com/en/billing/managing-billing-for-your-products/managing-billing-for-github-copilot/about-billing-for-github-copilot?params=ref-blog-how-to-use-github-copilot&ref=blog-how-to-use-github-copilot#:~:text=GitHub%20Copilot%20in%20your%20organization "Highlights: GitHub Copilot in your organization")); M365 Copilot: ~$30/user/mo (add-on) | Google Cloud pricing model (e.g. $ per query or seat via Vertex AI); Gemini itself no fixed price for chat |
  | **Adoption / Market** | ~80% share of public chat usage (as of Aug 2025) ( [\[15\]](https://www.techradar.com/pro/chatgpt-reigns-sovereign-in-the-ai-chatbot-market-share-as-microsoft-copilot-catches-up-on-perplexity#:~:text=Data%20from%20StatCounter%20covering%20July,far%20ahead%20of%20any%20competitor "Highlights: Data from StatCounter covering July,far ahead of any competitor")); used in >80% Fortune 500 ( [\[1\]](https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-enterprise/#:~:text=Since%20ChatGPT%E2%80%99s%20launch%20just%20nine,creative%20work%2C%20and%20much%20more "Highlights: Since ChatGPT’s launch just nine,creative work, and much more")) | Rapidly growing; favored for high-complexity tasks (esp. coding, data analysis) ( [\[19\]](https://www.techradar.com/pro/openai-models-are-the-favorites-for-enterprise-users-right-now-but-anthropic-isnt-far-behind#:~:text=CIOs%20prefer%20OpenAI%20for%20general,enterprises%20are%20turning%20away%20from "Highlights: CIOs prefer OpenAI for general,enterprises are turning away from")) | Copilot prominence rising: many large orgs (Toshiba, Dentsu, etc.) on board; 85% Fortune 500 use Microsoft AI ( [\[30\]](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-cloud/blog/2025/07/24/ai-powered-success-with-1000-stories-of-customer-transformation-and-innovation/?msockid=039e8bdc0ba064b42e529d2b0aae6555#:~:text=We%20have%20come%20a%20long,and%20customer%20satisfaction%2C%20according%20to "Highlights: We have come a long,and customer satisfaction, according to")) | Emerging; Gemini is #2 in brand recognition; 65% of Google Cloud customers use AI tools ( [\[6\]](https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning/introducing-gemini-enterprise#:~:text=This%20complete%2C%20AI,Figma%2C%20GAP%2C%20%205%20Gordon "Highlights: This complete, AI,Figma, GAP, 5 Gordon")); major clients (Figma, Gap) onboard |
  | **Example Customers** | Klarna, Canva, Block, Zapier, PwC ( [\[1\]](https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-enterprise/#:~:text=Since%20ChatGPT%E2%80%99s%20launch%20just%20nine,creative%20work%2C%20and%20much%20more "Highlights: Since ChatGPT’s launch just nine,creative work, and much more")) ( [\[22\]](https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-enterprise/#:~:text=,%E2%80%9D "Highlights: ,”")) | Novo Nordisk, Cox Automotive, Palo Alto Networks, IG Group ( [\[24\]](https://www.anthropic.com/news/driving-ai-transformation-with-claude#:~:text=The%20transformation%20was%20immediate%3A%20documentation,took%20months%20with%20external%20agencies "Highlights: The transformation was immediate: documentation,took months with external agencies")) ( [\[25\]](https://www.anthropic.com/news/driving-ai-transformation-with-claude#:~:text=The%20impact%20was%20immediate,9%2C000%20client%20deliverables%20to%20date "Highlights: The impact was immediate,9,000 client deliverables to date")) | Buckinghamshire Council ( [\[17\]](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-cloud/blog/2025/07/24/ai-powered-success-with-1000-stories-of-customer-transformation-and-innovation/?msockid=039e8bdc0ba064b42e529d2b0aae6555#:~:text=Council%20of%20the%20Year%20in,to%20achieve%20more%20with%20fewer "Highlights: Council of the Year in,to achieve more with fewer")), British Heart Foundation ( [\[50\]](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-cloud/blog/2025/07/24/ai-powered-success-with-1000-stories-of-customer-transformation-and-innovation/?msockid=039e8bdc0ba064b42e529d2b0aae6555#:~:text=144,to%20build%20a%20solution%20that "Highlights: 144,to build a solution that")), BNY Mellon ( [\[5\]](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2025/02/05/https-blogs-microsoft-com-blog-2024-11-12-how-real-world-businesses-are-transforming-with-ai/#:~:text=13,and%20the%20Azure%20ecosystem%20to "Highlights: 13,and the Azure ecosystem to")) | Figma, Gap, Macquarie Bank, Mercedes, GlaxoSmithKline (partnered with Google Cloud) |
  | **Strengths** | Powerful general intelligence; wide plugin ecosystem; mature support; widely adopted | Unmatched contextual capacity; emphasis on accuracy/safety; collaborative workspaces; strong code/data abilities | Seamless Office/GitHub integration; enterprise security; high developer productivity gains; established support and training | Deep multimodal AI; integrated with Google Cloud/Workspace; robust RAG/agent framework; big infrastructure scale |
  | **Weaknesses** | Closed model (no on-prem); context < Claude’s; initial concerns on bias/hallucination (improving); price | Smaller ecosystem; fewer third-party tools; model can be conservative; still catching up in popularity | Vendor lock-in in Microsoft stack; less flexible outside MS; earlier versions were buggy (improving); low user adoption rate reported | Newer to market; requires Google Cloud buy-in; cost can be high; concerns over Google’s data handling; model fine-tuning less transparent to customers |
  
